---
/**
 * Feature section — copy left, plugins demo right.
 *
 * See docs/feature-section.md. The block is step `content` and its height comes
 * from `16/9`, so the section fills about half a screen: enough to read from a
 * distance, not so much that the scroll stalls.
 *
 * THE FIRST OF THREE SECTIONS THAT READ AS ONE RUN, and the exception to
 * docs/layout.md § "One boundary, one shape". Plugins, Skills and CLIs draw NO
 * boundary of their own — no framed band, no card, no ground of their own.
 * Between the logo strip's closing rule and the voice section's opening one
 * there is nothing but the two rails and three blocks of content breathing at
 * the standard inset. Asked for by the maintainer on 2026-08-29: the frames and
 * the lines between these three were reading as boxes stacked in a column.
 *
 * WHAT THAT COSTS, AND WHY IT IS PAID HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE. The shared shell
 * exists so that no two sections meet in a way nobody chose. These three opt
 * out of it TOGETHER, as one run, so the property it protects still holds: the
 * run has exactly one boundary at each end, drawn by the neighbour, and the
 * joints inside it are the only joints on the page with no line at all — by
 * decision. A single section leaving the shell would be the old bug back.
 *
 * THREE THINGS ARE LOAD-BEARING AND EASY TO "TIDY" BACK IN:
 *
 *   - No `.section-bounds`. It is what drew the box.
 *   - No section background. The page has one ground and these three stand on
 *     it like everything else; painting one under this run would put a seam
 *     back at exactly the joints this change removed. See layout.css § "The
 *     page has ONE ground".
 *   - `<SectionTrack open />` on the SECTION, not `nested` inside a band. See
 *     the marker note below.
 *
 * Depth is the well inside the demo and hairlines. There are no shadow tokens
 * in this system, and no card frame here any more.
 */
import Container from "@/components/Container.astro";
import SectionTrack from "@/components/SectionTrack.astro";
import { PluginsDemo } from "@/components/plugins-demo/PluginsDemo";
---

<!--
  No shell: this section draws no boundary and no ground. See the note above
  for what that buys and what it costs.

  THE MARKER IS TRACKED ON THE SECTION ITSELF, and both halves of that matter:

  - not `nested` inside a band, because the tracked box has to TILE the
    document for the square to run without stopping. A band is held an inset
    inside its section, so the square would reach the band's bottom, then wait
    out `2 x --section-inset` of air before reappearing at the top of the next
    one — three short runs with two gaps, instead of one unbroken line.
  - `open`, because nothing is drawn under this section for the square to cross.
    An open section hands over on the rail it came down, so Plugins, Skills and
    CLIs are one continuous descent on the LEFT rail — which is what the
    maintainer asked for. Take `open` off and the square turns right along a
    rule that does not exist.
-->
<section id="features" class="relative flex flex-col">
  <SectionTrack open />
  <Container width="content" class="section-inset flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col">
    <!--
      No frame, no surface: the copy and the demo stand on the page itself,
      between the two rails. The inline padding stays, as the inset that keeps
      them off the rails; below `lg` the vertical air is `.section-inset`'s job,
      so the padding is `px` and not `p`.

      `lg:p-14` AND NOT `lg:px-14`, AND THAT IS NOT A LEFTOVER OF THE CARD.
      `aspect-ratio` sizes the BORDER box, so this block is 16/9 of the content
      column either way and the section's height does not depend on the figure.
      What the vertical padding decides is how much of that height the demo
      column gets, because the well beside the copy is `lg:h-full`. Dropping it
      with the card handed the well the whole of it, and the painting in the
      well grew with it - reported by the maintainer on 2026-08-29 against the
      build that removed the frame. The inline and block figures match on
      purpose: with no frame drawn, an uneven inset reads as the demo sitting
      off-centre in its own air.
    -->
    <div
      class="grid items-center gap-12 px-8 lg:aspect-[16/9] lg:min-h-[560px] lg:grid-cols-12 lg:p-14"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <!--
          Heading and body are one optical block: same size, separated by weight
          and ink alone. A size jump here would turn a sentence into a headline
          plus a subtitle, which is a louder shape than this section needs.
        -->
        <p class="text-[22px] leading-snug sm:text-[26px]">
          <span class="font-medium text-ink"
            >Plugins connect Jarvis to the tools you already use.</span
          >{" "}
          <span class="text-body"
            >Sign in once, and it can read your mail, find a file or start the
            music. When a connection stops working, it tells you which one and
            why.</span
          >
        </p>

        <!--
          A real link, and the one thing in this section that is focusable — the
          demo beside it is aria-hidden and every control in it is tabIndex -1.
          Ink, not an accent: docs/design.md retired the borrowed hue.
        -->
        <a
          href="#docs"
          class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[16px] font-medium text-ink underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
        >
          See every plugin
          <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:h-full">
        <PluginsDemo client:visible />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</section>
